## Putting it all together

The course covered: syntax, OOP, collections, lambdas, Stream, Optional. The final task exercises everything together.

## Model

```java
class Product {
    private final String name;
    private final double price;

    Product(String name, double price) {
        this.name = name;
        this.price = price;
    }

    String getName() { return name; }
    double getPrice() { return price; }
}
```

## Stream + Optional

```java
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Optional;

List<Product> products = List.of(
    new Product("A", 100),
    new Product("B", 200),
    new Product("C", 50)
);

double total = products.stream()
    .mapToDouble(Product::getPrice)
    .sum();
System.out.printf("Sum: %.1f%n", total); // 350.0

Optional<Product> expensive = products.stream()
    .filter(p -> p.getPrice() > 150)
    .findFirst();

expensive.ifPresentOrElse(
    p -> System.out.println(p.getName()),  // B
    () -> System.out.println("none")
);
```

## Breakdown

- `stream()` — from list
- `mapToDouble` — `DoubleStream`, `.sum()` returns `double`
- `filter` — select
- `findFirst` — `Optional<Product>`
- `ifPresentOrElse` — handle both cases

## Checks

- Class with `private final` fields
- Getters
- Stream for computation
- Optional for lookup
- No `null` in returns

## What if

- `get()` on empty Optional — `NoSuchElementException`.
- Mutable fields in model — Optional loses meaning.
- Forget `System.out.printf` — wrong formatting.

## Common mistake

`.map(Product::getPrice).sum()` — does not compile, need `mapToDouble`. `map` returns `Stream<Double>`, no `sum`.

## Summary

- Class + getters
- Stream: filter, mapToDouble, sum, findFirst
- Optional + ifPresentOrElse
- Composition — standard modern Java

